        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Incline walking matches easy running for general fitness and
            weight loss; running wins for speed and the top end.</strong> At a matched effort the
            calories are similar, both train the heart, and the real differences are impact, which
            muscles work, and how hard each can go. Beginners, heavier people and sore knees should
            start uphill; runners should keep running and walk uphill on easy days.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Neither delivers if the rails are doing part of the work or if the console calorie figure
            is doing the planning. Pick the one you will still be doing in six months, build it a
            step at a time, and see our
            <a href="/treadmill-workout-for-weight-loss/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">treadmill weight-loss plan</a>
